n's Charisma and free spirit which  complements his own stoic and individual  nature and really even though Zoro  walked his path alone if he hadn't  joined up with his captain he wouldn't  have survived the next Monumental step  in Zara's character growth is on the  baratier when he goes face to face with  mihawk arguably one of the best moments  in the entire series he's utterly  defeated but the warlord still sees  something important in Zorro even though  he still clearly lacks the power he has  the strength of will to grow and become  stronger and so the exchange between  these two Swordsmen actually foreshadows  many of Zorro's later Feats and his  growth as a character for example mihawk  defeats him with a tiny knife much like  the knife that Zorro uses at the  beginning of wano to escape his captors  Zorro Witnesses mihawk slicing a whole  ship in half a feat that Zorro is more  than capable of after the time Skip and  mihawk even refers to Zoro as a frog in  a well which is kind of similar to the  English saying of a small fish in a big  pond and then later on fisherman Island  Zara would actually use the exact same  sentence to hyozu the overly confident  greatest swordsman of Fishman Islands  later in Ireland Park and loc Town Zorro  comes to respect Luffy much much more  when he confronts arlong he sees just  how far Luffy himself is willing to go  for someone he considers his nakama and  in loketown he sees Luffy's fearlessness  in the face of death and how he's  willing to die if it meant that he's  working towards achieving his dream  again remember these are things that  Zorro values immensely as well on water  7 we really see Zorro step into the role  of the first mate for the very first  time when Luffy and usop fight over the  fate of the going Mary the rest of the  true are devastated Zorro however is the  glue that keeps them all together his  cool-headed stoic demeanor are crucial  in a situation like this when everyone's  emotions are really riled up he occupies  the difficult position and does what  must be done to maintain the sanctity of  the straw hats and Luffy's honor as a  captain he really understands just how  difficult his conflict is for Luffy but  at the same time even as Nami urges for  compassion zaro understands that the  crew must remain loyal to Luffy and Zoro  also refuses to allow Usopp to rejoin  while deflecting with humor and Antics  he'll only allow Luffy to let him board  the ship once again if he issues a  genuine apology for his misdeeds really  without zoro's strength and conviction  the crew may have fractured permanently  here on water 7. in the next Arc for the  bark we get the single most important  Zorro moment in the entire Series so far  nothing happens when the entirety of the  crew is incapacitated Kuma strikes a  bargain with Zorro the warlord will  spare Luffy's life and the rest of the  crew if Zara agrees to take on all the  pain that Luffy suffered during the  battle on top of Zorro's own already  severe strain from fighting ryuma and  oars this is the ultimate instance of  Zoro shouldering Luffy's burdens and  acting as a first mate and moreover  despite being terribly wounded he stands  with pride as he declares that nothing  happened Zorro doesn't do the things  that he does for credit he has complete  satisfaction in knowing that he's done  his duty and the right thing though it's  important to say that in this scene too  it shows Zorro's character flaw of  trying to take on everything by himself  and really it's the same with becoming  the world's greatest swordsman he's not  doing it to gain cloud or recognition in  the world he simply wants to prove his  strength to himself and no one else at  least as far as we know now one thing  that I think people Overlook is that  during the two-year time skip Zorro  demonstrated just how loyal he really is  to Luffy arguably even more than on  Thriller bark in order to become strong  longer and help fight for Luffy's dream  he's sacrificing his own pride and begs  dracul mihawk the person he wants to  take down to take him in as a student  Zorro began as a character with one  single goal he wanted to prove his own  strength but eventually he found that  through dedication and loyalty he could  find an even greater Purpose By fighting  not only for his own goal but for that  of Luffy and all the other straw hats  together as well he has unlocked his  true strength and potential strength  enough to become the world's greatest  swordsman for someone else so this  unbridled power isn't what makes Zoro  such a beloved character it's not just  his badass fights there are plenty of  characters who offer that kind of action  and so the real reason that people love  Zoro so much are his honor his  compassion and his altruism when Luffy  found him Zorro hadn't been crucified as  a test of his own will he was doing it  to save an innocent little girl and even  though Zorro walked a lonely road in  pursuit of his goal he never truly  walked alone his dream was not just his  it was inherited so really Zoro has  never really fought only to prove his  strength to himself but he fought to  prove his strength to kuwina and Luffy  and everyone who's dear to him so  similar to Luffy more than a character  Zoro is meant to portray an ideal that  through discipline loyalty honor we just  don't lift ourselves up but lift up  everyone around us and so the beauty of  zoro's character is that he shows us  that real strength and purpose comes  from unwavering dedication to others and  even then there is still so much more  detail in Nuance within Zara's character  especially for his character Arc with  Luffy I have a whole video breaking it  down in even more detail right here
 

